<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bantu peoples</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bantu-speaking</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bantu peoples are the large family of peoples speaking Bantu languages, spread across Central, East and Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Their expansion over many centuries carried agriculture and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-working">iron-working</a> across much of the continent. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo Empire</a> was founded by Bantu-speaking Kongo people in the lower Congo region.</p></div>
